<title>RUSSIA: Russian minister against mazut export curbs - agency.</title>
<headline>Russian minister against mazut export curbs - agency.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian Economy Minister Yevgeny Yasin is opposed to any restrictions on exports of fuel oil (mazut) during the 1996-1997 winter heating season, Interfax news agency quoted him as saying on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;I am against any quotas,&quot; it quoted him as saying, adding that Yasin had also said that slapping a tariff on mazut exports would violate Moscow's loan agreement with the International Monetary Fund.</p>
</text>
